---
import Docs from '../../layouts/Docs.astro';
import Icon from '../../components/Icon.astro';

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/?$/, '/');
const prompt =
  'XML, all fields: Trades (Executions + Closed Lots), Open Positions (Lot), Cash Transactions, Prior Period Positions, Statement of Funds, Account Information, Financial Instrument Information';
const sections = [
  { name: 'Trades', options: 'Executions + Closed Lots', why: 'Every sale with the exact lot it closed: acquisition date and cost.', req: true },
  { name: 'Open Positions', options: 'Lot (not Summary only)', why: 'One row per purchase lot with its open date — Schedule FA A3 needs one row per lot.', req: true },
  { name: 'Cash Transactions', options: 'Detail', why: 'Dividends, interest and US tax withheld for Schedules OS, FSI, TR and Form 67.', req: true },
  { name: 'Account Information', why: 'Account number, opening date and IBKR entity for Schedule FA A2.', req: false },
  { name: 'Prior Period Positions', why: 'Daily price of every position — exact Schedule FA peak values with no outside price data.', req: false },
  { name: 'Statement of Funds', why: 'Running cash balance — the true peak cash for Schedule FA A2.', req: false },
  { name: 'Financial Instrument Information', why: 'Full company names, ISIN and issuer country.', req: false },
  { name: 'Cash Report', why: 'Opening and closing cash, used if Statement of Funds is missing.', req: false },
  { name: 'Change in Dividend Accruals', why: 'Ex-dates, so each dividend is matched to the lots that earned it.', req: false },
  { name: 'Corporate Actions', why: 'Splits, mergers and spin-offs are flagged for review.', req: false },
];
const config = [
  ['Format', 'XML'],
  ['Period', 'Any — you choose dates each time you run it'],
  ['Date format', 'yyyyMMdd (default) or yyyy-MM-dd'],
  ['Time format', 'HHmmss (default)'],
  ['Include canceled trades', 'No'],
  ['Everything else', 'Leave at default'],
];
const years = [
  { label: 'AY 2026-27', sub: 'FY 2025-26', cy: ['1 Jan 2025', '31 Dec 2025'], fy: ['1 Apr 2025', '31 Mar 2026'] },
  { label: 'Tax year 2026-27', sub: 'Income-tax Act 2025', cy: ['1 Jan 2026', '31 Dec 2026'], fy: ['1 Apr 2026', '31 Mar 2027'] },
];
const toc = [
  { id: 'ai', label: 'Quick way: Configure with AI' },
  { id: 'manual', label: 'Create it by hand' },
  { id: 'sections', label: 'Sections' },
  { id: 'settings', label: 'Delivery settings' },
  { id: 'run', label: 'Run it twice' },
  { id: 'faq', label: 'Questions' },
];
---
<Docs title="Flex Query Guide · IBKR India Tax" description="Create the IBKR Activity Flex Query this tool needs, step by step." crumb="Flex Query guide" toc={toc}>
  <span class="badge accent"><Icon name="book" size={14} />Setup guide</span>
  <h1>Create your IBKR Flex Query</h1>
  <p class="lead">
    A Flex Query is a report template you build once in IBKR and run for any dates. It is the only IBKR export with lot-level
    detail — each purchase's date and cost, and which lot each sale closed — which is exactly what Schedule FA and capital gains need.
  </p>
  <div class="facts">
    <span class="fact"><Icon name="clock" size={16} /><span><b>10 minutes</b>, once</span></span>
    <span class="fact"><Icon name="file-table" size={16} /><span><b>1 query</b>, XML format</span></span>
    <span class="fact"><Icon name="calendar" size={16} /><span><b>2 runs</b> per return</span></span>
  </div>

  <section id="ai">
    <h2><span class="h-icon"><Icon name="sparkle" size={18} /></span>Quick way: Configure with AI</h2>
    <p class="sec-lead">IBKR can build the query from one description of up to 200 characters. Each prompt generates a whole new query, so use this single prompt rather than several.</p>
    <ol class="vsteps">
      <li>
        <div>
          <b>Open Configure with AI</b>
          <span class="path-chip">Performance &amp; Reports <Icon name="chevron-right" size={12} /> Flex Queries <Icon name="chevron-right" size={12} /> Configure with AI</span>
        </div>
      </li>
      <li>
        <div>
          <b>Paste this prompt and click Generate Flex Query</b>
          <div class="prompt">
            <div class="prompt-head"><b>Prompt · {prompt.length}/200 characters</b><button class="btn sm" data-copy={prompt}><Icon name="copy" size={16} /><span>Copy</span></button></div>
            <p>{prompt}</p>
          </div>
          <p>Saying “all fields” matters: without it the AI picks a short default list that leaves out <b>Open Date Time</b>, each lot's purchase date.</p>
        </div>
      </li>
      <li>
        <div>
          <b>Review the generated query</b>
          <div class="kv check-kv">
            <div class="kv-row"><span>Format</span><b>XML</b> </div>
            <div class="kv-row"><span>Trades → Options</span><b>Execution and Closed Lots</b></div>
            <div class="kv-row"><span>Open Positions → Options</span><b>Lot</b></div>
            <div class="kv-row"><span>Trades and Open Positions fields</span><b>include Open Date Time</b></div>
          </div>
          <p>If anything differs, click <b>Edit Manually</b>, fix it, and press <b>Select All</b> in any section with a short field list.</p>
        </div>
      </li>
      <li>
        <div>
          <b>Optional: add two more sections</b>
          <p>In <b>Edit Manually</b>, add <b>Change in Dividend Accruals</b> (ex-dates for matching dividends to lots) and <b>Corporate Actions</b> (flags splits), each with <b>Select All</b>.</p>
        </div>
      </li>
      <li>
        <div>
          <b>Save</b>
          <p>The period it sets (for example “Last Business Day”) doesn't matter — you pick dates each time you run it. After upload, the tool lists any field that is still missing.</p>
        </div>
      </li>
    </ol>
  </section>

  <section id="manual">
    <h2><span class="h-icon"><Icon name="file-table" size={18} /></span>Or create it by hand</h2>
    <ol class="vsteps">
      <li>
        <div>
          <b>Open Flex Queries</b>
          <span class="path-chip">Client Portal <Icon name="chevron-right" size={12} /> Performance &amp; Reports <Icon name="chevron-right" size={12} /> Flex Queries</span>
        </div>
      </li>
      <li><div><b>Create an Activity Flex Query</b><p>Click <b>+</b> next to Activity Flex Query and name it, for example <code>india-tax</code>.</p></div></li>
      <li><div><b>Add each section below</b><p>In each section's popup set the options shown, click <b>Select All</b> for the fields, then <b>Save</b>.</p></div></li>
      <li><div><b>Apply the delivery settings</b><p>Set the format to XML, keep the other defaults, and save the query.</p></div></li>
    </ol>
  </section>

  <section id="sections">
    <h2><span class="h-icon"><Icon name="check-circle" size={18} /></span>Sections</h2>
    <p class="sec-lead">Three are required. The rest turn approximations into exact figures.</p>
    <div class="sec-grid">
      {sections.map((s) => (
        <div class:list={['sec', { req: s.req }]}>
          <div class="sec-top"><b>{s.name}</b><span class:list={['badge', { accent: s.req }]}>{s.req ? 'Required' : 'Recommended'}</span></div>
          {s.options && <span class="opt">Options: {s.options}</span>}
          <p>{s.why}</p>
        </div>
      ))}
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="settings">
    <h2><span class="h-icon"><Icon name="info" size={18} /></span>Delivery settings</h2>
    <div class="kv">
      {config.map(([k, v]) => <div class="kv-row"><span>{k}</span><b>{v}</b></div>)}
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="run">
    <h2><span class="h-icon"><Icon name="calendar" size={18} /></span>Run it twice</h2>
    <p class="sec-lead">
      Schedule FA reports the <b>calendar year</b>; capital gains, dividends and the foreign tax credit report the <b>financial year</b>.
      IBKR allows 365 days per run, so run the saved query with two custom date ranges and download each XML.
    </p>
    <div class="run-grid">
      {years.map((y) => (
        <div class="run-card">
          <header><b>{y.label}</b><span class="badge">{y.sub}</span></header>
          <div class="run-line"><Icon name="calendar" size={18} /><span><b>{y.cy[0]} → {y.cy[1]}</b>Run 1 · Schedule FA</span></div>
          <div class="run-line"><Icon name="calendar" size={18} /><span><b>{y.fy[0]} → {y.fy[1]}</b>Run 2 · Capital gains, dividends, foreign tax credit</span></div>
        </div>
      ))}
    </div>
    <div class="callout accent">
      <Icon name="arrow-right" />
      <div>
        <b>Then drop both files into the tool.</b>
        <p>Click the run (▶) icon on the query, choose Custom Date Range, run, and download. Overlapping periods are merged without double counting.</p>
      </div>
      <a class="btn primary sm" href={base}>Open the tool</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="faq">
    <h2><span class="h-icon"><Icon name="info" size={18} /></span>Questions</h2>
    <div class="faq">
      <details>
        <summary>Why not the regular Activity Statement?<Icon name="chevron-right" size={18} /></summary>
        <p>It summarises positions per stock and leaves out each lot's purchase date and the lot every sale closed. Schedule FA needs one row per lot and capital gains need the true holding period of each lot.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>How far back can I export?<Icon name="chevron-right" size={18} /></summary>
        <p>Flex Queries cover the four previous calendar years plus the current one. Lots bought earlier still appear in Open Positions with their original open date and cost.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>What about purchases before 2020?<Icon name="chevron-right" size={18} /></summary>
        <p>The tool's SBI rate archive starts in January 2020. For older dates it asks you to type in the SBI TT buying rate, which your bank or CA can provide.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>I trade options or futures. Are they covered?<Icon name="chevron-right" size={18} /></summary>
        <p>No. Only stocks and ETFs are computed. Other trades are listed as warnings so you can report them separately with your CA.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>Is my file safe?<Icon name="chevron-right" size={18} /></summary>
        <p>The XML contains your account number and full trading history. This site has no server: the file is read by JavaScript in your browser, and the page's security policy blocks it from contacting any other site. You can turn off Wi-Fi after the page loads and it still works.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>Can I see the output first?<Icon name="chevron-right" size={18} /></summary>
        <p>Yes — on the <a href={base}>tool page</a>, choose “See it with sample data”. It is a fictional account.</p>
      </details>
    </div>
  </section>
</Docs>
